_Dog.png?7c4980 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></div></div></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>200</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>0.72%\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Entities\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Entities\">&gt; Entities</span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Enemy_Spawns_.28Interior.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Enemy_Spawns_(Interior)\">Enemy Spawns (Interior)</span></h3>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Enemy Name</th>\n<th>Rarity</th>\n<th>Max Spawned</th>\n<th>Power Lvl.</th>\n<th>Spawn Chance\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Droop\" title=\"Droop\">Droop</a></td>\n<td>160</td>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>51.95%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bracken</td>\n<td>46</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>14.94%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Butler</td>\n<td>40</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>12.99%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Masked</td>\n<td>30</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>9.74%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Maneater</td>\n<td>25</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>8.12%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Smile\" title=\"Smile\">Smile</a></td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>0.5</td>\n<td>1.62%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Girl</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>0.65%\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h3><span id=\"Enemy_Spawns_.28Exterior.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Enemy_Spawns_(Exterior)\">Enemy Spawns (Exterior)</span></h3>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Enemy Name</th>\n<th>Rarity</th>\n<th>Max Spawned</th>\n<th>Power Lvl.</th>\n<th>Spawn Chance\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Droop\" title=\"Droop\">Droop</a></td>\n<td>165</td>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>91.67%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Eyeless Dog</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>8.33%\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Lore\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Lore\">&gt; Lore</span></h2>\n<p>While there are no loggable items or data terminals found on <b>Xenphir</b>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Droop\" title=\"Droop\"><b>Droop</b></a> has a unique Bestiary Entry that provides context for what happened to this moon.\n</p>\n<table class=\"article-table mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Droop <span style=\"padding-left:0.5em;\">&#x2060;</span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table style=\"border: 15px solid #8E8E83; font-size: 135%; font-family: Tomorrow; color: #01A801; border-spacing: 0px;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"padding: 25px; background-color: #151515;\">DROOP<br /><br />Sigurd's danger level: uhhhh I dnot know but thsi sou nds horrifyign<br /><br />Scientific name: Vorictus-detoma<br /><br />The Vorictus-detoma, garnered the name \u201cDroop\u201d due to its drooping appearance. Its arms, legs and neck are exceptionally long, likely due to the body deformation which happens in the process of a Droop\u2019s creation.<br /><br />The Droop is not officially classified as a non-human creature, while it no longer possesses the humanity it once did, it technically is still human. Only with the effects of prolonged exposure to V-Radiation.<br /><br />V-Radiation is an incredibly rare phenomenon and has previously had very adverse and unexplainable effects on creatures and places, often leading to deformation and destruction. Sightings of V-Radiation were extremely rare up until the Grand war where it was occasionally used to cause mass destruction. However, even by supporters of the use of biological warfare, it was greatly frowned upon due to its cruel and otherworldly effects often rendering places uninhabitable.<br /><br />While there have not been many encounters, the majority of the Droop were likely everyday civilians affected during the war. <br />Direct exposure to gamma or beta rays of V-Radiation vaporises the average unprotected human, leaving behind what can only be described as a shadow or a memory where they once were. It is not certain what exactly it is that they leave behind but it is thought to no longer be alive. However there have been rumors of these shadows stalking or moving in the dark.<br />When exposed to alpha rays of V-Radiation you won\u2019t immediately notice any harmful effects aside from a slight headache or brief dizziness. But from the moment of exposure you have been infected with a unique type of radiation sickness. While it doesn\u2019t break your DNA, it does change it which only becomes noticeable after a few days. Skin might start feeling heavy and organs might move around during a very painful process. If the infected is still alive 13 days past the first exposure, changes start happening to the brain, often noting highly irregular brainwaves. From this point onwards it is only a husk of its former self. While it is on a technical level not death, this is what we consider the moment of death. The person is unrecoverable and the body is deformed to an unrecognisable level where the skin and muscles resemble a droopy obsidian. <br /><br />There has not been any research from this point onwards.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Trivia\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Trivia\">&gt; Trivia</span></h2>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Gallery\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Gallery\">&gt; Gallery</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:XenphirLand.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"The ship on Xenphir.\"><img alt=\"The ship on Xenphir.\" src=\"/images/thumb/XenphirLand.jpg/120px-XenphirLand.jpg?261d01\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/XenphirLand.jpg/180px-XenphirLand.jpg?261d01 1.5x, /images/thumb/XenphirLand.jpg/240px-XenphirLand.jpg?261d01 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">The ship on Xenphir.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:XenphirDistant.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A distant view of Xenphir.\"><img alt=\"A distant view of Xenphir.\" src=\"/images/thumb/XenphirDistant.jpg/120px-XenphirDistant.jpg?5989c2\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/XenphirDistant.jpg/180px-XenphirDistant.jpg?5989c2 1.5x, /images/thumb/XenphirDistant.jpg/240px-XenphirDistant.jpg?5989c2 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A distant view of Xenphir.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:XenphirMatter.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A purple and starry crater.\"><img alt=\"A purple and starry crater.\" src=\"/images/thumb/XenphirMatter.jpg/120px-XenphirMatter.jpg?9573d9\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/XenphirMatter.jpg/180px-XenphirMatter.jpg?9573d9 1.5x, /images/thumb/XenphirMatter.jpg/240px-XenphirMatter.jpg?9573d9 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A purple and starry crater.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:XenphirMain.jpg\" class=\"image\" ti